Changes made for the PICO WebSpatial Academy kit (2026-09-24):
  - package.json: React 19 + Vite 8 + TypeScript 6 to match labs/VERSIONS.md; SDK pinned to 2.0.0
    instead of workspace:*; port 5501; scripts dev / dev:xr / build / build:xr.
  - vite.config.ts: react({ jsxImportSource: '@webspatial/react-sdk' }) passed explicitly.
    Upstream relies on plugin-react reading tsconfig, which Vite 8 (oxc) does not do.
    Added the @pico/theme alias and fs.allow for ../../theme.
  - index.html, eager-lean.html, xr-monitor.html: data-theme="light", icon, manifest link.
  - public/app.webmanifest + public/icons/ (kit icons): name, short_name, start_url, scope,
    display minimal-ui, icons, xr_main_scene.
  - src/main*.tsx: import the kit's PICO theme.
  - src/spatial-app.tsx: <Model> renders only inside a WebSpatial runtime (a flat browser shows a
    placeholder instead of an unknown <model> tag, which logged a React console error), and PICO
    gets public/modelasset/avocado.glb (from labs/p3) instead of cone.usdz (a visionOS format).
  - UPSTREAM-README.md is the original README, unchanged. Its pnpm workspace setup steps do not
    apply here.
